    <briefdescription>
<para>Interface for commit operations in a file store. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_file_store_commit" kindref="compound">FileStoreCommit</ref></computeroutput> class provides interfaces for committing changes, expiring old snapshots, dropping partitions, and retrieving commit metrics.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Direct file-system commits support append-only and primary-key tables on non-object-store paths. Object-store paths require REST catalog commit mode: enable it with <computeroutput><ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_commit_context_builder_1ae9b915cd4fd9a12757ca11239ec2fbc6" kindref="member">CommitContextBuilder::UseRESTCatalogCommit()</ref></computeroutput>, call <computeroutput><ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_file_store_commit_1af7d78ade944ce09c77fc5c5fa4668881" kindref="member">Commit()</ref></computeroutput> or <computeroutput><ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_file_store_commit_1a7588411adfc60796e3ef42d976caab93" kindref="member">FilterAndCommit()</ref></computeroutput>, and then retrieve the request with <computeroutput><ref refid="classpaimon_1_1_file_store_commit_1a5ae2fb04ea79c56cfdd2aee86737bd5a" kindref="member">GetLastCommitTableRequest()</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
